# DocsWatcher's own exclusions. docs/18-excluding-paths.md.
#
# This repository is a deprecation database: it has to contain every retired model name, in its
# records, its fixtures and the tests that prove the scanner finds them. None of that is product
# code calling an API, so none of it is scanned.
/knowledge/
/study/

# The release smoke test calls a retired model on purpose, to prove the published binary finds it.
/.github/workflows/release.yml

# Tests and demo text name retired models on purpose: to prove they are found, and to show a
# visitor what happens. They call nothing.
/app/src/test/
/cli/src/test/
/engine/src/test/
/web/tests/
/relay/test/
/notify/test/
/web/app/components/TryAssistant.vue
/web/app/pages/agents.vue
# The MCP server's tool description and input examples name models; it calls no API.
/cli/src/main/java/dev/docswatcher/cli/McpServer.java
# Documentation, and check_api's own messages, name models as examples.
/docs/
/README.md
/CHANGELOG.md
/web/engine/checkApi.ts
